archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2294907Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2304414Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2404411Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2414231Z ^[[0m
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2415075Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2415933Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2416378Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2416753Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2418142Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2418685Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2419040Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2419646Z    if you are ready to continue.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2419889Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2420300Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2420916Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2421787Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2422235Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2422430Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2422694Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2422992Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2423220Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2423633Z    can use Nix.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2423790Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2423913Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2424108Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2424440Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2425003Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2426688Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2426888Z I will:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2427223Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2427471Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2428249Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2428968Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2429418Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2429738Z  - install Nix in /nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2430040Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2430496Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2430962Z    /root
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2443830Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2444623Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2455383Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2456135Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2456637Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2457562Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2458248Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2475797Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2476378Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2486802Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2487566Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2488027Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2488413Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2488718Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2488997Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2489220Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2489764Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2490170Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2490365Z If you would like to
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2490845Z see the output, try like this:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2491194Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2492256Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2492743Z   $ sh ./install-nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2492918Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2492953Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2493219Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2499508Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-23T14:58:18.2499991Z been installed on this system.
